Fillets: the opposite contact's parameter at an OnSame end, on a periodic
contact curve whose range is a whole period, stays at the end being updated
instead of going to the other end a period off (mitcad#1359).

Update brings the parameter where the contact meets the face at the end
into the interference's range [uf, ul] with ElCLib::InPeriod. A boss's
foot rounded on a plate's top up to the plate's sides, on the body MitCad's
sketch and extrusions build: the blend's contact on the boss's cylinder
runs a whole period, from -3.6e-15 to 2 pi, and at the vertex where the
cylinder's seam starts it meets the face at the end at -3.7e-15, a little
below uf. InPeriod took it to 2 pi - 3.7e-15: the contact's range
collapsed to [2 pi, 2 pi], the cap's end on the blend lay a period off its
other end, and the cap was sought round the whole torus ("echec calcul
intersection" at radius 3; at 1 and 6 an invalid result). Where the range is a whole
period, a parameter within the curve's resolution of the far end that is a
period off the end being updated is taken at that end.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the boss's foot rounded
with 1, 3 and 6 on the body MitCad's sketch and extrusions build
(MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES): valid, the material added as the exact one within
1e-6 of it.

Upstream: new.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
@@ -243,6 +243,23 @@ static bool Update(const occ::handle<Adaptor3d_Surface>& fb,
     // blend rolling on an edge ends where the edge does, on the face at the
     // end, its contact curves bounded there.)
     const double tolw = std::max(Precision::PConfusion(), ct->Resolution(Precision::Confusion()));
+    // A parameter on a periodic curve brought into [uf, ul]: where the range
+    // is a whole period (a contact all round its axis, both ends one point),
+    // a point at the end being updated, a little past it, stays at that end
+    // instead of going to the other end a period off (the range collapsed).
+    const auto inRange = [&](const double t) {
+      double       aT = ElCLib::InPeriod(t, uf, ul);
+      const double T  = ct->Period();
+      if (isfirst && ul - aT <= tolw && std::abs(aT - T - uf) <= tolw)
+      {
+        aT -= T;
+      }
+      else if (!isfirst && aT - uf <= tolw && std::abs(aT + T - ul) <= tolw)
+      {
+        aT += T;
+      }
+      return aT;
+    };
     for (i = 1; i <= nbp; i++)
